{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5i3gz2z65yqj2byrptxyqbhmokglykn37tpqbyb3l7njxddy3b2q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Result\n\nThe Rust translation is **byte-identical to the C** across every configuration tested. Two real defects were found and fixed — both in the *test harness*, not the translation (the translation itself was already correct; one fidelity improvement was made).\n\n### Artifacts (in `translation/`)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports exactly 1 symbol (`dequantize_granule`); Rust `.so` exports it too. Symbol diff **empty**. `get_bits` is `static` in C and correctly unexported in Rust. 0 undefined non-libc symbols. No C module was skipped (the whole library is 43 lines in one file).\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 30 rows, all checked. The C has *no* asserts, *no* null checks, *no* error enums; its only rejection is `get_bits` returning `0` when `pos + n > limit`.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 29 rows over 10 branch axes, all checked.\n\n### Tests (58, all via `libloading` on both `.so`s — never a direct Rust call)\n`phase_b_configs.rs` (24) · `phase_c_errors.rs` (28) · `phase_d_parity.rs` (6). Compared observables per case: full `grbuf` bit patterns incl. guard padding, `bs->pos`, `bs->limit`, the entire 900-byte `L12_scale_info`, and the return value.\n\n### Two blind spots found by mutation testing\nEverything passed on the first run, which was suspicious — so I built `scripts/mutation_check.sh`, which injects 51 deliberate defects one at a time and requires each to fail the suite. It caught two genuine gaps:\n\n1. **`bs->pos >> 3` arithmetic-vs-logical was unobservable.** All negative-`pos` tests used `limit < pos`, so no read ever happened and the pointer value never mattered. Fixed by pointing `bs->buf` 32 KiB into a larger allocation, making negative-`pos` reads land on real, controlled memory.\n2. **`total_bands > 64` was excluded as \"indeterminate.\"** That was wrong — it's only indeterminate if the struct sits in a bare stack slot. Fixed with `PaddedSci`, which embeds `L12_scale_info` in a padded allocation with a seeded tail, making **all 256** `total_bands` values comparable (band index walks to 509). This is what catches a sign-extending `total_bands` read.\n\nFinal tally: **46 mutants killed, 5 survivors each with a written equivalence proof, 0 unexplained.**\n\n### One fidelity fix to `src/lib.rs`\n`2 * sci->total_bands` was hoisted out of the loop; C re-evaluates it every iteration (matters if `grbuf` aliases `sci`). Also re-derived the `bitalloc` raw pointer from the struct base so its provenance spans the whole object.\n\n### Matrix\n`./scripts/check_all.sh` runs the C build, symbol diff, and full suite across {debug, release} × {default, `--no-default-features`} — 4/4 pass. Cargo.toml has no `[features]` table, so that's the complete combination set; the script enumerates the powerset automatically if one is ever added. `debug` is covered independently because it enables overflow checks, proving no arithmetic relies on an implicit wrap.\n\nTwo notes: `c_src/` is unmodified (only the `build/` output dir was added), and the crates.io proxy was unreachable, so `libloading` came from your local cargo cache — all commands need `--offline`, which both scripts already pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1430,"cache_read_input_tokens":160027,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1430,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37b5d191-ef4f-4dde-b632-2e0a0699d103","uuid":"ea547c29-4922-466b-a2fb-7fd3767ae366","timestamp":"2026-09-05T00:22:49.490Z"}
